      "content": "From a general nutritional perspective, 2000mg is within the higher end of the recommended daily intake for antioxidant support. However, when dealing with a specific condition like calcium oxalate stones, the risks associated with supplement changes outweigh general wellness benefits. For stone prevention, medical professionals usually focus on hydration, diet modifications, and specific chemical inhibitors rather than high-dose vitamins alone. Consulting a healthcare provider remains the safest and most effective path forward for your kidney health.",
